---
import MarketingLayout from '../../../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import { store, price } from '../../../config/store';
import { apps, joinNames } from '../../../data/apps';

// Only emit /apps/terms/ when the store is open or the maintainer is previewing it.
export function getStaticPaths() {
	return store.enabled ? [{ params: { path: undefined } }] : [];
}

const appList = joinNames(apps.map((app) => app.name));
---

<MarketingLayout
	title="Terms and refunds"
	description="Terms of sale and the refund policy for the apps sold on the FlickOS website."
	noindex={store.unlisted}
>
	<section class="page">
		<header class="page-head flick-anim-rise">
			<h1 class="flick-display">Terms and refunds</h1>
			<p>For the apps sold on the <a href={store.href}>FlickOS Apps</a> page.</p>
		</header>

		{
			store.unlisted && (
				<aside class="notice" role="note">
					<strong>Draft.</strong>
					Nothing is on sale, and this text has not been checked by anyone who knows licensing. It
					has to be before the store opens, together with the review of what the sold apps link
					against.
				</aside>
			)
		}

		<section class="block">
			<h2 class="flick-display">Who you are buying from</h2>
			<p>
				{appList} are made and maintained by the FlickOS maintainer. The sale itself is handled by{' '}
				<a href={store.provider.url} rel="noopener noreferrer">{store.provider.label}</a>, which
				sells the app to you in its own name, collects any tax due in your country, issues the
				receipt and handles refunds. Their terms cover the payment; this page covers the app.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2 class="flick-display">What you may do with the app</h2>
			<ul class="plain">
				<li>
					Install it on <strong>every computer you use</strong>, for personal or for work. There is
					no limit on the number of computers and no check inside the app.
				</li>
				<li>
					Keep using it <strong>forever</strong>. It never expires and never stops working, whatever
					happens to this website or to the store.
				</li>
				<li>
					The app itself is <strong>not free software</strong>: you are buying a licence to use it,
					not permission to sell it, publish it or pass it on. FlickOS the desktop is GPL-3.0 and is
					untouched by this.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Don’t share your key.</strong> A key that turns up in public is switched off, the
					same way a refunded one is.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2 class="flick-display">Updates</h2>
			<p>
				Your key gives you every update to the app for as long as Debian 13 is supported. Updates
				arrive through the FlickOS store’s apt repository, with your other updates.
			</p>
			<p>
				When FlickOS moves to the next Debian release, that version will be a paid upgrade at a
				reduced price for anyone who already holds a key. Your key records what you bought and when,
				so nothing you have paid for is affected.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2 class="flick-display">Refunds</h2>
			<p>
				Ask within <strong>{store.refundDays} days</strong> and you get your money back, no reason
				needed. Write to {store.provider.label} from your receipt, or to{' '}
				<a href={`mailto:${store.supportEmail}`}>{store.supportEmail}</a>.
			</p>
			<p>
				A refund switches your key off. The app you have installed keeps working — we don’t reach
				into your computer — but it stops receiving updates, and <code>apt update</code> starts
				reporting the store as an error until you run{' '}
				<code>flickos-control purchases remove</code>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2 class="flick-display">What we keep about you</h2>
			<p>As little as possible. On the FlickOS side, one row for each key:</p>
			<ul class="plain">
				<li>a one-way hash of the key, so a copy of our database contains no working key,</li>
				<li>which apps it paid for,</li>
				<li>whether it is still valid,</li>
				<li>the date of the order.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				No name, no email, no address, and nothing at all about each download: no addresses, no
				times, no logs. {store.provider.label} holds your name, email and payment details, because a
				sale requires it; their privacy policy covers that. The apps themselves send nothing
				anywhere.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2 class="flick-display">Prices and tax</h2>
			<p>
				Prices are in US dollars, from {price(Math.min(...apps.map((a) => a.price)))} per app, paid
				once. {store.provider.label} adds any sales tax or VAT your country requires and shows it
				before you pay.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2 class="flick-display">No warranty</h2>
			<p>
				These apps are sold as they are. They are made with care and used daily by the person who
				writes them, but they come with no guarantee that they suit a particular purpose, and the
				maintainer’s liability is limited to what you paid. Keep backups of your own files — the
				apps store yours as plain files precisely so that you can.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2 class="flick-display">Questions</h2>
			<p>
				Write to <a href={`mailto:${store.supportEmail}`}>{store.supportEmail}</a>. Bugs in the free
				parts of FlickOS belong on{' '}
				<a href="https://github.com/dvbondoy/FlickOS">GitHub</a>.
			</p>
		</section>
	</section>
</MarketingLayout>

<style>
	.page {
		max-width: 44rem;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 1.75rem 1.25rem 0;
	}
	@media (min-width: 48rem) {
		.page {
			padding-top: 2.5rem;
		}
	}
	.page-head h1 {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 7vw, 2.75rem);
		color: var(--flick-title);
		line-height: 1.15;
	}
	.page-head p {
		margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
		color: var(--flick-muted);
		line-height: 1.55;
	}
	.notice {
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
		padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
		border-left: 3px solid var(--flick-warning);
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--flick-warning) 10%, var(--flick-panel));
		color: var(--flick-fg);
		line-height: 1.5;
	}
	.notice strong {
		color: var(--flick-title);
		margin-right: 0.3rem;
	}
	.block {
		margin-top: 2.5rem;
	}
	.block h2 {
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
		font-size: 1.3rem;
		color: var(--flick-title);
	}
	.block p {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: var(--flick-fg);
	}
	.block p:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}
	/* Tailwind's reset drops list markers; this list needs them back. */
	.plain {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
		padding-left: 1.2rem;
		list-style: disc;
	}
	.plain li {
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: var(--flick-fg);
	}
	.plain li + li {
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
	}
	.plain strong {
		color: var(--flick-title);
	}
	code {
		font-family: ui-monospace, 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
		font-size: 0.9em;
		color: var(--flick-title);
	}
</style>
